<title>UK: C&amp;W EGM tripped up by 2nd class post.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W EGM tripped up by 2nd class post.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British telecommunications group Cable &amp; Wireless Plc said on Friday it had rescheduled an extraordinary general meeting to approve ending its partnership with German utility and telecommunications group Veba AG.</p>
<p>C&amp;W had scheduled a meeting for today. But the letter for the meeting was posted by second-class mail inadvertently, meaning there was insufficient notice for shareholders, the company said. A meeting was held but was unable to approve the Veba transaction.</p>
<p>The rescheduled meeting is expected to take place on March 24.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
